  "notes": "Cash basis county. Statement receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Total column of Exhibit D (p4); roll-forward on fund balances 9,269,021 -> 8,538,296 (ties; transfers in 1,404,931 = out 1,404,931). Ending cash = Equity in Pooled Cash and Cash Equivalents, ending investments = Designated Investments (p3); no beginning cash printed. Balance sheet from the governmental funds Balance Sheet - Cash Basis Total column (p3; equals the Statement of Net Position p1). Noxious Weed spending is natural resources/conservation (user rule). Detail: budget-and-actual schedules for the major funds (General p5-6, Road p7, Inheritance Tax p8, American Rescue Plan p9) and the nonmajor combining schedule per fund column (pp10-12; Fair Building has no activity). The nonmajor budget schedule (Schedule 3, pp13-15) prints only fund totals and is not recorded (same money as the combining schedule). General Fund Taxes 6,032,323 split into Property Taxes 5,659,448 + Motor Vehicle Tax 372,875 from the General column of Exhibit D (adds exactly); Inheritance Tax Fund Local 421,134 split into Inheritance Tax 400,648 + Miscellaneous 20,486, and American Rescue Plan Local 865,942 into Federal Grants 865,332 + Interest 610, from their Exhibit D columns (each adds exactly). General Fund State 104,326 / Local 606,625 do not tie to the Exhibit D column lines (Intergovernmental 151,569 etc.), so kept as printed. Budget lines with no actual (General Fund transfers in budget 400,000; Inheritance Tax transfers out budget 400,000; American Rescue Plan General Government budget 1,800,334) not recorded. Read pages 1-15 of 15"
}
